.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_RAND-TEST-RAND 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_RAND-TEST-RAND
.Nd The test EVP_RAND implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for a test generator through the
.Sy EVP_RAND
API. This generator is for test purposes only, it does not generate
random numbers.
.Ss Identity
"TEST-RAND" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_RAND_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
The supported parameters are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqstate" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_STATE Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
These parameter works as described in
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 .
.It \(dqstrength" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_STRENGTH Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqreseed_requests" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_RESEED_REQUESTS Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqreseed_time_interval" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_RESEED_TIME_INTERVAL Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqmax_request" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_RESEED_REQUESTS Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmin_entropylen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_MIN_ENTROPYLEN Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmax_entropylen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_MAX_ENTROPYLEN Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmin_noncelen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_MIN_NONCELEN Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmax_noncelen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_MAX_NONCELEN Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmax_perslen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_MAX_PERSLEN Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmax_adinlen" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_MAX_ADINLEN Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqreseed_counter" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_RESEED_COUNTER Ns ) <unsigned integer>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 ,
except that they can all be set as well as read.
.It \(dqtest_entropy" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_TEST_ENTROPY Ns ) <octet string>
Sets the bytes returned when the test generator is sent an entropy
request.
The current position is remembered across generate calls.
If there are insufficient data present to satisfy a call, an error is
returned.
.It \(dqtest_nonce" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_TEST_NONCE Ns ) <octet string>
Sets the bytes returned when the test generator is sent a nonce request.
Each nonce request will return all of the bytes.
.It \(dqgenerate" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_GENERATE Ns ) <integer>
If this parameter is zero, it will only emit the nonce and entropy data
supplied via the aforementioned parameters.
Otherwise, low quality non-cryptographic pseudorandom output is
produced.
This parameter defaults to zero.
.El
.Sh NOTES
A context for a test generator can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_RAND *rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "TEST-RAND", NULL);
 EVP_RAND_CTX *rctx = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, NULL);
.Ed
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
 EVP_RAND *rand;
 EVP_RAND_CTX *rctx;
 unsigned char bytes[100];
 OSSL_PARAM params[4], *p = params;
 unsigned char entropy[1000] = { ... };
 unsigned char nonce[20] = { ... };
 unsigned int strength = 48;

 rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "TEST-RAND", NULL);
 rctx = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, NULL);
 EVP_RAND_free(rand);

 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_uint(OSSL_RAND_PARAM_STRENGTH, &strength);
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_RAND_PARAM_TEST_ENTROPY,
                                          entropy, sizeof(entropy));
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_RAND_PARAM_TEST_NONCE,
                                          nonce, sizeof(nonce));
 *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
 EVP_RAND_instantiate(rctx, strength, 0, NULL, 0, params);

 EVP_RAND_generate(rctx, bytes, sizeof(bytes), strength, 0, NULL, 0);

 EVP_RAND_CTX_free(rctx);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 ,
.Xr EVP_RAND 3
.Sh HISTORY
This functionality was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
